
 = Lantern Moth =

 The lantern moth is an invented insect used here only as test text . It rests by day under bark and flies at dusk toward pale stones .

 = = Habits = =

 It feeds on the nectar of night flowers and is said to hum when it lands . No record of it exists outside this file .

 = Copper Bridge =

 The Copper Bridge is a footbridge in an imagined river town . It was built of riveted plates in a single summer and painted green each spring .

 = = Repairs = =

 After a flood the middle span was raised by two metres , and the town held a fair on the day it reopened .

 = = = Fair = = =

 The fair sold bread , rope and small brass bells .

 = Salt Orchard =

 A salt orchard is a grove of short trees grown near the sea in a story told for children . Its fruit is sour and keeps for a year .

